    "message": "ci(hygiene): install the runtime dependencies the import needs\n\nKUYEN_GIT_HISTORY_RECOVERY_AND_RELEASE_17, commit 11. The previous attempt installed the\npackage with `--no-deps`, so `import kuyen` still failed on the runner (it needs `PyYAML` at\nimport time) and `version agrees` kept failing. Reproduced locally in a clean venv: with\n`--no-deps` the import raises `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'yaml'`; with the declared\ndependencies it prints `version agrees: 0.3.0`.\n\nThe step is now a plain editable install. The assertion is unchanged and the job still has no\nway to pass while `VERSION` and `kuyen.__version__` disagree.",
